## Features by role

### Public pages
Home, Register (choose Organiser or Participant), Login, Access Denied.

### Organiser
| Page | What it does |
|---|---|
| Dashboard | Totals (events, upcoming events, enrolments, next event), upcoming events with enrolments per event, past events |
| My Events | List with Edit, Delete and links to Categories, Enrolments and Results |
| Create / Edit event | Name, description, date, start time, venue (location), distance, event type, optional banner image |
| Add venue | Name, address, city, province, optional coordinates |
| Categories | Add, edit and delete age or distance categories for an event |
| Enrolments | Every participant enrolled for the event, with category, bib number and colour-coded status |
| Results | Enter status, finish time, position and distance covered per participant. Saving publishes the result. Locked until the event date has passed |

### Participant
| Page | What it does |
|---|---|
| Events (home) | Upcoming events as cards, with filters for search, type, province and date |
| Event details | Full information, banner image and categories, each with an Enrol button |
| My Enrolments | All enrolments with status badges and a Cancel button |
| My Results | Event, date, category, finish time and position such as "47th of 312 finishers" |
| Profile | Update name, phone and date of birth, and upload a profile picture |

Statuses are colour coded: **Confirmed** (green, stored as `Enrolled`), **Cancelled** (red), **Did not finish** (amber) and **Did not start** (grey).

## API overview
The API implements the 27 endpoints from the Part 1 plan (see `/docs`), plus two upload endpoints added in Part 3: `POST /api/events/{id}/banner` and `POST /api/participants/me/picture`. All endpoints are visible and testable in Swagger, which shows each endpoint's purpose, the data it expects, its responses and its access rule (public, any logged-in user, Organiser only or Participant only).

