## Security notes
- Passwords are hashed with BCrypt and never stored or returned in plain text.
- JWT tokens carry the user's ID and role. Protected endpoints require a valid token, and role and ownership are checked in the API.
- Secrets are not in the repository. The Azure key lives in User Secrets. Anyone running the project supplies their own.
- Anyone can register as an Organiser (the brief asks users to choose their role). A production system would need an approval step.

## Known limitations and future improvements
- Replaced images stay in Azure (old files are not deleted).
- The API does not block enrolling in past events or entering results before an event ends. The MVC app enforces this in the interface only.
- Positions are typed in by the Organiser, not calculated from finish times.
- Sessions are held in memory, so restarting the MVC app logs everyone out.
- No email verification, password reset or Organiser profile page.

